{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"106514","commit":"481ee9d8cd64812b96a7fff5d7d8f64ce4161a01","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The exception type was changed from `ResourceNotFoundException` to `AliasesNotFoundException`, but there is no evidence of corresponding changes in the exception handling logic or documentation. This could lead to confusion or unhandled exceptions if other parts of the system expect `ResourceNotFoundException`. Additionally, the error message was changed from `\"required alias [test_2] does not exist\"` to `\"aliases [test_2] missing\"`, but there is no evidence of corresponding changes in logging, monitoring, or alerting systems to accommodate this new format. This introduces architectural drift and poses a risk of undetected issues if other parts of the system rely on the old error message for specific actions.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/cluster/metadata/MetadataIndexAliasesServiceTests.java-DST-DST_UPDATE-7566-7592-StringLiteral","path":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/cluster/metadata/MetadataIndexAliasesServiceTests.java","srcDst":"DST","content":"\"aliases [test_2] missing\"","nodeType":"DST_UPDATE","treeType":"StringLiteral","descendantSimpleNames":[],"startLine":163,"startLineOffset":52,"endLine":163,"endLineOffset":78,"length":27,"subs":[]},{"id":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/cluster/metadata/MetadataIndexAliasesServiceTests.java-DST-DST_UPDATE-7356-7380-SimpleName","path":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/cluster/metadata/MetadataIndexAliasesServiceTests.java","srcDst":"DST","content":"AliasesNotFoundException","nodeType":"DST_UPDATE","treeType":"SimpleName","descendantSimpleNames":["AliasesNotFoundException"],"startLine":160,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":160,"endLineOffset":36,"length":25,"subs":[]},{"id":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/cluster/metadata/MetadataIndexAliasesServiceTests.java-SRC-SRC_UPDATE-7543-7583-StringLiteral","path":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/cluster/metadata/MetadataIndexAliasesServiceTests.java","srcDst":"SRC","content":"\"required alias [test_2] does not exist\"","nodeType":"SRC_UPDATE","treeType":"StringLiteral","descendantSimpleNames":[],"startLine":163,"startLineOffset":52,"endLine":163,"endLineOffset":92,"length":41,"subs":[]},{"id":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/cluster/metadata/MetadataIndexAliasesServiceTests.java-SRC-SRC_UPDATE-7274-7299-SimpleName","path":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/cluster/metadata/MetadataIndexAliasesServiceTests.java","srcDst":"SRC","content":"ResourceNotFoundException","nodeType":"SRC_UPDATE","treeType":"SimpleName","descendantSimpleNames":["ResourceNotFoundException"],"startLine":159,"startLineOffset":14,"endLine":159,"endLineOffset":39,"length":26,"subs":[]}]},{"comment":"The introduction of `IndicesAliasesResponse` and the replacement of `AcknowledgedResponse` across various parts of the codebase are intended to provide more detailed feedback for alias operations. However, several issues arise from these changes:\n- The constructor `IndicesAliasesResponse::new` does not validate the `actionResults` list for null or empty values, potentially leading to NullPointerExceptions during serialization/deserialization.\n- There is a lack of logging or error handling in the `writeTo` and `readFrom` methods for `actionResults`, which could result in silent failures during serialization/deserialization.\n- The `build` method does not handle cases where `actionResults` is null or empty, leading to unexpected behavior.\n- The `IndicesAliasesResponse.AliasActionResult` class includes a method `getStatus` that returns incorrect status codes if the `error` object is null or has an unexpected status.\n- The private constructor in `IndicesAliasesResponse.AliasActionResult` asserts the `indices` list is not empty but does not provide any logging or error handling if the condition fails, leading to silent failures during object construction.\n- The `toXContent` method does not handle cases where the `error` object is null or has unexpected fields, resulting in incomplete or incorrect serialization.\n- The private constructor in `IndicesAliasesResponse.AliasActionResult` initializes the `indices`, `action`, and `error` fields without any validation or error handling, leading to inconsistent object states.\n- The `buildSuccess` and `buildRemoveError` methods do not validate the `indices` list for null or empty values, causing unexpected behavior.\n- The implementation of `IndicesAliasesResponse.build(request.getActionResults())` is unspecified in the technical mapping, risking incomplete or inconsistent data being returned.\n- The change from `AcknowledgedResponse.TRUE` to `IndicesAliasesResponse.build(request.getActionResults())` assumes that `build(request.getActionResults())` will correctly handle successful operations without a detailed specification.\n- The change from `AcknowledgedResponse.FALSE` to `IndicesAliasesResponse.NOT_ACKNOWLEDGED` assumes that `NOT_ACKNOWLEDGED` will correctly represent failed operations without a detailed specification.\n- The update of method signatures and listener types to accept `IndicesAliasesResponse` does not address potential issues with existing implementations that depend on the old response or listener types, risking runtime errors or unexpected behavior.\n- The replacement of `ResourceNotFoundException` with `AliasesNotFoundException` does not ensure all error handling mechanisms are updated, introducing architectural drift and potential unhandled exceptions.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/core/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/core/ml/utils/MlIndexAndAliasTests.java-DST-SEMANTIC_CONTEXT-4893-4952-MethodInvocation","path":"x-pack/plugin/core/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/core/ml/utils/MlIndexAndAliasTests.java","srcDst":"DST","content":"withResponse(IndicesAliasesResponse.ACKNOWLEDGED_NO_ERRORS)","nodeType":"SEMANTIC_CONTEXT","treeType":"MethodIn